Dear Jordan,

Please find the framework for your proposal below.

Timeline
- Proposal due: 30 October 2026. Contract award: mid-December 2026.
- Installation from 1 February 2027. Go-live before 1 October 2027, so we are stable
  well before Black Friday.

Commercial terms
- Fixed price for hardware, software, installation and project management.
- Milestone payments: 25% at signature, 35% at mechanical completion, 40% at go-live
  acceptance.
- Budget: around 6.5 million, including all allowances.

Allowances
Several areas cannot be known before signature: the legacy WMS interfaces, the
floor slab, the fire authority's sprinkler decision, the product data clean-up and
the marketplace volumes. For each of these, show a separate, clearly named allowance
in your price with the hours behind it. Do not hide them in your rates, and do not
exclude them: we would rather see the risk priced than find it later as a change
request.

Customer responsibilities
Please list in your proposal everything you assume we provide or decide, with the
date you need it. Several of these are still open on our side: the D365 sandbox and
integration method, single sign-on, power to the drop positions, the carton range,
building access, the mezzanine, returns, and acceptance testing.

Parcel carriers
- Our parcel carrier contract is out to tender. We will choose two carriers in the
  first quarter of 2027, so we can't yet tell you which carriers, or their label
  and API formats. We will request test and production credentials from the winners
  and pass them on.

Support
- 24/7 support with a 2-hour response time from October to December, business hours
  for the rest of the year.

Kind regards,
Oliver Grant
